cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Silicon Mitosis: self-dividing current filaments in SKY130 silicon and dimension-dependent division in active matter"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "counfield"
    website: "https://counfield.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/berkmec/silicon-mitosis"
url: "https://counfield.com/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-15"
abstract: >-
  Model and simulation study of current filaments in a wide, ballasted SKY130 nFET (reduced 4 K model built from the
  foundry BSIM4 card with ngspice). A filament splits when the drain voltage at its centre reaches the lowest voltage at
  which the latched state exists; this gives a parameter-free split law w_s = 2 lambda ln[lambda / (lambda - lambda_c)],
  validated against pre-registered simulations. Also: dimension-dependent division of active Cahn-Hilliard droplets up to a
  6D hypercube, phase-space plasma holes, and equation discovery from data. The original room-temperature quantum goal is
  documented as currently unsuccessful.
keywords:
  - SKY130
  - current filaments
  - pattern formation
  - self-replication
  - Cahn-Hilliard
  - active droplets
  - reaction-diffusion
  - open-source PDK
